From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fizzy macos worker <fizzy-macos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] web: a keyboard's correction replaces the typed word

A phone keyboard corrects the word before the caret, but the hidden input stayed empty and
every beforeinput/compositionend was sent as new text, so "im" became "imI'm". TextInput keeps
the word typed since the last space in the hidden input, caret at its end, and turns an
insertReplacementText (its target range, or the selection the keyboard made, when a range is
empty as it is for an input) or a composition that rewrote the word into backspaces and the
new text. A pointer, a navigation key, a delete it cannot follow, a blur or another field
clears the word.
---
 src/backends/web.js | 159 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 128 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

